    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0247" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9–2746: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-09-27T20:00:00-04:00">September 27,
                            1946—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>803. Emb[assy] is requested supply info[rmation] on points mentioned below as
                    background helpful to Dept in considering Chinese problems.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Original positions, significant changes of position and most recent stands
                        of Kmt,<anchor n="96" xml:id="d124-f1"/> CCP<anchor n="97" xml:id="d124-f2"
                        /> and other political elements re number <pb facs="0248" n="238"
                            xml:id="pg238"/> of seats to be assigned each in State Council and re
                        number of votes necessary to exercise veto.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Whether Kmt actually ratified PCC<anchor n="98" xml:id="d124-f3"/>
                        decisions without reservation as announced by Central News. We realized that
                        the PCC decisions met with strong opposition in the CEC<anchor n="99"
                            xml:id="d124-f4"/> but we would like to know the basis for the CCP
                        charge that Kmt ratification was qualified. Please also endeavor to find out
                        character of reservations, whether open or covert.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clayton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
